      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2720335202,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "I was about to approve this but... @guyharris Why is SOME_FUNCTIONS_ARE_INLINE there?  It looks like there was some cleanup to remove #defines (which I support), but I don't see why we can't just always have the inline functions, since that's what the code is enforcing anyway.\nAlso, file is no longer part of Wiretap",
          "author": {
            "id": 8399509,
            "username": "mmann78",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Michael Mann",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/fad119898ba16a3f8be2f765dcff399098444abd4f85a04d4c3ef415a2bbe3d9?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/mmann78"
          },
          "created_at": "2025-08-30T12:20:15.658Z",
          "updated_at": "2025-08-31T16:43:11.350Z",
          "system": false,
          "noteable_id": 411428346,
          "noteable_type": "MergeRequest",
          "project_id": 7898047,
          "resolvable": true,
          "resolved": true,
          "resolved_by": {
            "id": 6792385,
            "username": "AndersBroman",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "AndersBroman",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/132fb48f26018ea9516aea909144af3c3a94eaf2ba477efaa9a232abe80d322c?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/AndersBroman"
          },
          "resolved_at": "2025-08-31T16:43:11.350Z",
          "confidential": false,
          "internal": false,
          "imported": false,
          "imported_from": "none",
          "noteable_iid": 21125,
          "commands_changes": {}
        },
        {
          "id": 2720338947,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "I would _gently_ vote in favor of retaining the possibility of building without `SOME_FUNCTIONS_ARE_INLINE`, at least for the time being... In my experiments today, it seems useful for adjusting the implementation of our `ws_buffer_*` routines to maximize sensitivity for fuzzing, which is how I came to discover the problem and prepare this MR.  (The current implementation has unfortunate properties which lead to the fuzzer being unable to locate certain classes of defect in the wiretap parsers.)  I'm not sure at this stage whether the more-sensitive `Buffer` is worth putting in the repository or will only live in a private patch I keep locally; Perhaps I can just move `SOME_FUNCTIONS_ARE_INLINE` into a private patch too, if we decide to not keep it here in the repo. :smile:",
          "author": {
            "id": 7889756,
            "username": "dariusd0",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "dariusd0",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
